  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final package keeps S2 at a 5% test limit with per-model disclosure to purchasers and regulators but no public publication, satisfying both red lines on disclosure. S3 requires new-unit shut-off immediately and a 72-month retrofit with a feasibility alternative; S4 requires built-in suppression or an approved equivalent at 36 months. S5 sets a mandatory 8/100k model-level recall trigger with 24-hour customer incident notices, while S1 requires 24-hour incident reporting to regulators."
